      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Global trade is definitely undergoing significant shifts, moving away from purely efficient, cost-driven globalization. A major driver of this change is geopolitical tension, leading countries to prioritize supply chain resilience and national security over minimal costs. This trend is fueling reshoring, nearshoring, and \"friend-shoring,\" where companies move production closer to home or to allied nations. Ultimately, the balance between economic efficiency and strategic risk is being re-evaluated worldwide.",
